MLLM description: The wire-haired fox terrier is a small to medium-sized dog with a distinctive appearance characterized by its wiry, dense coat that is typically short and close to the body. This breed has a compact, muscular build with a strong, arched neck and a level back. The head is elongated with a slightly rounded skull, a long muzzle, and a black nose. The ears are small, triangular, and set high on the head, often folded over at the tips. The eyes are dark and expressive.

In terms of color patterns and markings, wire-haired fox terriers can come in various combinations of white, black, and tan. The most common pattern is a white base with black and tan markings, including a black saddle or patch on the back, a tan blaze down the center of the face, and tan markings on the legs and chest. However, there are also solid white, black, and tan variations. The coat is usually smooth and shiny, with a slight wave or curl, giving it a distinctive texture.

The size and proportions of the wire-haired fox terrier are relatively consistent across individuals. They stand around 10-12 inches tall at the shoulder and weigh between 14-18 pounds. Their body is well-proportioned
